From 4f05e8261edaf963da8cceaf526666d85df1dd3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: op-bench-framework <op-bench-framework@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:34:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 216/252] fix(op-bench-tests): stop fabricating a
 session-scoped pypto package

The focused op-bench test file imported pypto through a fake package that
lacked __portable_only__ and was never removed from sys.modules, so later
test files in the same pytest session took the classic frontend branch and
failed (10 failed / 1416 passed on the canonical full suite at 140c88446).

- import the real pypto package instead; the canonical runner exports
  PYPTO_X_PORTABLE_ONLY=1 and this file selects the same frozen portable-only
  mode (os.environ.setdefault) when collected outside that harness;
- add test_real_pypto_package_survives_op_bench_imports: sys.modules['pypto']
  must be the real module with __portable_only__, pypto.op_bench must be the
  real submodule, and importing pypto.frontend must take the portable-only
  branch (the fake package raised AttributeError there);
- acceptance: 2 passed (both with and without the env var), op_bench+core_ir
  36 passed, op_bench+execution_matmul+portable_bootstrap 72 passed, 27
  focused tests passed.
